# Sensitive paths — maintainer-authored, review required before merge.
#
# THIS IS ABOUT THE PATH, NOT THE PERSON. It applies to maintainers writing
# their own code, not only to outside contributions. A solo maintainer shipping
# unreviewed auth at 2am is the same risk as anyone else, and a rule that only
# binds strangers is a rule about trust rather than about safety.
#
# Two failure modes it exists to catch, both real and both from this repo:
#   - A new environment secret on a money path. A variable that does not exist
#     yet reads as the empty string, so a check gated on it FAILS OPEN unless the
#     secret is deployed strictly before the code that reads it.
#   - A fix that looks right and does not close the hole. See #446: requiring the
#     `admin` scope would have authorised every agent, because public
#     registration grants `admin` to all of them.
#
# CODEOWNERS only REQUESTS review. To make it binding, enable "Require review
# from Code Owners" in branch protection on `main` — without that, this file is
# documentation, not a gate.
#
# Every path below was verified to exist when this file was written. A
# CODEOWNERS rule pointing at a path that does not exist silently protects
# nothing.

# Authentication and credential validation.
/src/auth/                              @DealAppSeo
/src/middleware/auth.ts                 @DealAppSeo

# Authorization services — routes mounted before the global auth middleware do
# their own checks here, which makes these the highest-consequence files in the
# repo.
/src/services/stake-authorization.ts    @DealAppSeo
/src/services/bounty-authorization.ts   @DealAppSeo

# Payout and reward paths.
/src/routes/bounties.ts                 @DealAppSeo
/src/engine/repid-update.ts             @DealAppSeo

# Delegated authority — mint, revoke, and the effective-authority calculation
# that gates spending.
/src/services/principal-grants.ts       @DealAppSeo
/src/services/effective-authority.ts    @DealAppSeo

# Key custody. This decrypts custodied agent wallet private keys.
/src/services/agent-key-crypto.ts       @DealAppSeo

# CI configuration — a workflow change can exfiltrate secrets or disable a gate.
/.github/workflows/                     @DealAppSeo
/.github/CODEOWNERS                     @DealAppSeo
